# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Audiobooks ignore list (EXAMPLE / REFERENCE FILE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `ignored/audiobooks.yaml` (drop the `.example` suffix)
# and uncomment / edit entries below as needed. The real `audiobooks.yaml`
# is gitignored so personal library decisions don't leak into the repo.
#
# Each entry is a path prefix. Any audiobooks-pass warning whose `path`
# field starts with one of these (followed by `/` or end-of-string,
# case-insensitive, separator-normalized) gets silently dropped from
# `output/audiobooks/warnings.json` (and counted in the run summary).
#
# Get paths from `output/audiobooks/warnings.json`. Most audiobook warnings
# use the `<Author>/<Book>` path shape.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Silence a single book ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drops every warning under this book's folder. Useful for a book with
# known missing chapters or a chapter naming inconsistency you've decided
# to keep.
# - J.R.R. Tolkien/The Lord of the Rings
# - Terry Pratchett/Discworld 41

# ── Silence by category ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drop ALL warnings under a category folder.
# - Other Audible
# - Book On CD

# ── Silence a whole author ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rare — usually only when you have a single author's catalog where every
# book has the same recurring issue.
# - Some Author
